## Claim
Text: "Joe and Jill Biden's income has increased recently."
Claim author: Kitty Freed
Claim date: October 18, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Joe Biden and Jill Biden release federal income tax returns covering a year shortly before October 2020?
Answer: Yes, the search result indicates that Joe Biden released federal income tax returns for 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, and 2019, with the 2019 return covering the year most shortly before October 2020.

Source URL: http://www.disclosures.org/joe-biden-financial-disclosures/

### What was the combined reported income of Joe Biden and Jill Biden on their 2019 federal tax return?
Answer: According to the source, Joe and Jill Biden's joint 2019 federal tax return reported approximately $985,000 of adjusted gross income (AGI), on which they paid almost $300,000 in federal taxes, resulting in an effective tax rate of 29.5%.

Source URL: https://www.cpapracticeadvisor.com/2020/09/30/biden-2019-tax-returns-show-high-income-and-high-tax-rate/40527/

### What was the combined reported income of Joe Biden and Jill Biden on their 2018 federal tax return?
Answer: According to the search result, Joe and Jill Biden "reported income of more than $11 million in 2017 and more than $4.5 million in 2018, much of it from book deals." Therefore, their combined reported income on their 2018 federal tax return was more than $4.5 million.

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-election/biden-releases-2019-tax-returns-ahead-first-debate-n1241387

### What was the combined reported income of Joe Biden and Jill Biden on their 2017 federal tax return?
Answer: According to the source, Joe and Jill Biden reported approximately $11 million in adjusted gross income on their 2017 federal tax return.

Source URL: https://www.cnbc.com/2019/07/09/joe-biden-releases-tax-returns-during-2020-democratic-primary.html

### Did Joe Biden file a U.S. Senate or candidate financial disclosure report for the year 2019, and if so, what income range did it list?
Answer: Yes, Joe Biden filed a candidate financial disclosure report in 2019 while running for the 2020 Democratic presidential nomination. According to the source, the disclosure showed that he and Jill Biden "took in more than $15 million since leaving the Obama White House," including a "$8 million book deal," over "$4 million" from approximately 50 speaking appearances, at least "$2.7 million in business income" from his publicity tour and writing, "$540,000" from his role at the University of Pennsylvania's Penn Biden Center, and at least "$700,000" from Jill Biden's speaking engagements.

Source URL: https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/biden-earned-millions-after-leaving-white-house-financial-reports-shows

### What were the primary sources of income reported by Joe and Jill Biden in 2019, such as book royalties, speaking fees, pension, or government salary?
Answer: According to the source, the primary sources of income reported by Joe and Jill Biden in 2019 included: Joe Biden's income from the University of Pennsylvania, a book tour, and a federal pension, as well as Jill Biden's income from Northern Virginia Community College. The article also notes that the Bidens' substantial income in prior years (2017 and 2018) came "much of it from book deals," with their 2019 taxable income totaling about $945,000.

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-election/biden-releases-2019-tax-returns-ahead-first-debate-n1241387

### How did Joe and Jill Biden's reported 2019 income compare numerically to their reported 2018 income?
Answer: According to the search result, Joe and Jill Biden reported about $945,000 in taxable income in 2019, compared to more than $4.5 million in 2018. This means their 2019 income was significantly lower—not higher—than their 2018 income, contradicting the claim that their income "has increased recently."

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-election/biden-releases-2019-tax-returns-ahead-first-debate-n1241387

### How did Joe and Jill Biden's reported 2018 income compare numerically to their reported 2017 income?
Answer: According to the source, Joe and Jill Biden reported income of "more than $11 million in 2017 and more than $4.5 million in 2018, much of it from book deals," meaning their 2018 income was lower than their 2017 income by more than $6.5 million.

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-election/biden-releases-2019-tax-returns-ahead-first-debate-n1241387

### Did Jill Biden receive any salary or earned income from her employer (such as Northern Virginia Community College) during the years 2017 through 2019?
Answer: Yes, according to the search result, "Jill Biden earned more than $90,000 in both 2017 and 2018 for working as a professor at Northern Virginia Community College." The source confirms she received salary from this employer during at least 2017 and 2018, though it does not specifically address 2019.

Source URL: https://nypost.com/2019/07/09/joe-and-jill-biden-have-made-15m-since-leaving-white-house/

### Has any reputable fact-checking organization or news outlet (e.g., PolitiFact, FactCheck.org, The New York Times, The Washington Post) publicly reported the trend in Joe and Jill Biden's income in the years leading up to October 2020?
Answer: Yes, Voice of America (VOA) reported on the trend in Joe and Jill Biden's income, noting that "Former U.S. Vice President Joe Biden and his wife, Jill, earned more than $15 million in the two years after Biden left government in early 2017," with the couple earning "about $11 million in 2017 and $4.58 million in 2018," largely from speaking engagements and book payments. This reporting supports the claim that their income increased significantly in the years leading up to October 2020, as their earnings rose substantially after leaving the vice presidency compared to their government salary.

Source URL: https://www.voanews.com/a/usa_us-politics_biden-and-wife-made-more-15m-after-leaving-office/6171514.html

## Final Judgement
## Summary of Key Findings

The evidence clearly establishes a declining income trend for Joe and Jill Biden in the years immediately preceding October 2020. Their reported income was approximately $11 million in 2017, more than $4.5 million in 2018, and approximately $985,000 (AGI) in 2019. This represents a consistent year-over-year decrease, not an increase. While one source notes that their post-White House earnings were substantially higher than their government salary, this comparison refers to the period after leaving the vice presidency in early 2017, not a "recent" increase as of October 2020.

## Missing Information

No additional information is needed. The evidence is clear and comprehensive enough to reach a conclusion.

## Conclusion

The claim that "Joe and Jill Biden's income has increased recently" is directly contradicted by the documented tax return data. Their income decreased substantially from 2017 (~$11M) to 2018 (~$4.5M) to 2019 (~$985K). The most recent trend clearly shows a decline, not an increase. Therefore, the claim is refuted.

`refuted`

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The tax return data for Joe and Jill Biden shows a clear declining income trend in the years leading up to October 2020, directly contradicting the claim that their income had "increased recently." They reported approximately $11 million in adjusted gross income in 2017, more than $4.5 million in 2018, and about $985,000 in 2019—representing a consistent year-over-year decrease ([NBC News](https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-election/biden-releases-2019-tax-returns-ahead-first-debate-n1241387), [CPA Practice Advisor](https://www.cpapracticeadvisor.com/2020/09/30/biden-2019-tax-returns-show-high-income-and-high-tax-rate/40527/)). While their post-White House earnings were substantially higher than their government salary, this comparison reflects the period after leaving the vice presidency in early 2017, not a "recent" increase as of the claim's date. The documented year-over-year decline from 2017 through 2019 definitively refutes the assertion.